# Cobalt Tapes: website

A one-page brand site for Cobalt Tapes. It's plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript, with no build step, no frameworks and nothing to pay for. It's ready for GitHub Pages.

```
cobalt-tapes/
├── index.html              ← all page text lives here
├── README.md
├── assets/
│   ├── css/style.css       ← colours, fonts, layout
│   ├── js/config.js        ← YOUR SPOTIFY LINK GOES HERE
│   ├── js/main.js          ← animations (no need to touch)
│   ├── fonts/              ← Archivo font + its licence
│   └── images/             ← hero.jpg, satin.jpg, lines.jpg, chrome.jpg, haze.jpg, favicon.svg
└── tools/
    └── generate_images.py  ← optional: makes new abstract artwork
```

---

## 1. Before you publish: add your Spotify link

Open `assets/js/config.js` and replace the placeholder:

```js
spotifyUrl: "https://open.spotify.com/user/YOUR-PROFILE-ID"
```

Every Spotify button and link on the page uses this one value.
To get your link in Spotify, open your profile, then tap **••• → Share → Copy link to profile**.

> Optional: `index.html` also has `href="https://open.spotify.com/"` as a fallback for the rare visitor with JavaScript turned off. If you'd like, use find-and-replace to put your link there too.

