## 3. Changing things

### Text
All copy is in `index.html` and labelled by section (`1. HERO`, `2. ABOUT`, and so on). Edit the words between the tags.

### Images
Replace any file in `assets/images/` with your own image **under the same file name**, and the layout picks it up. Recommended sizes:

| File | Where it shows | Shape | Suggested size |
|---|---|---|---|
| `hero.jpg` | band through the logo | wide | 2400 × 1500 |
| `satin.jpg` | About section | portrait 4:5 | 1600 × 2000 |
| `lines.jpg` | full-width strip | very wide | 2400 × 700 |
| `chrome.jpg` | collage, left | portrait 4:5 | 1400 × 1750 |
| `haze.jpg` | collage, right | landscape 16:10 | 2400 × 1400 |

Images are cropped to fit, so any size close to these works. Keep each file under ~600 KB so the page loads fast (squoosh.app is free and works well for this). If you swap in a photo, also update its `alt="..."` text in `index.html` to describe the new image.

Good sources of free photos that need no attribution: **Unsplash** (unsplash.com) and **Pexels** (pexels.com). Searches like *long exposure*, *smoke*, *texture*, *chrome* and *blue light* suit the look.

### Colours
At the top of `assets/css/style.css`:
```css
--void: #09090B;     /* page background */
--charcoal: #141418;
--cobalt: #0047AB;   /* brand blue */
--silver: #C6CAD2;
--muted: #8B8C96;
--white: #F2F3F5;
```

### New abstract artwork (optional)
The current images were generated by `tools/generate_images.py`, so they're original and need no credit. To make a fresh set (Python 3 required):
```bash
pip install numpy scipy pillow
python tools/generate_images.py --seed 42
```
Each different seed gives a new variation.

